  "notes": "- The readme says contributors can create drafts (readme.txt:173), but the code does not allow it. create_post_from_args requires publish_posts before anything else (includes/MCP/Server.php:7513), so Contributors cannot create posts through MCP at all.\n- The readme and the admin wizard disagree about local sites. The readme FAQ says Claude Desktop works with a local site (readme.txt:163). The wizard says localhost will not work for Claude Desktop (templates/admin/partials/connection-wizard.php:99, 195).\n- Any user with edit_posts can connect, not just admins. Authors and contributors can authorise their own AI clients, which then get every tool their role allows. There is no admin setting to restrict this, only a code filter.\n- The destructive-action confirmation is off by default. The `confirm` argument is added to every destructive tool's schema in tools/list, so an AI client can send confirm:true on its first call. No MCP destructiveHint annotations are sent.\n- Undo system: many write tools return a single-use, 7-day undo token. Admins can also undo from the Activity page. This is unusual and goes beyond the checklist.\n- A leftover plaintext 'api_key' is written to bcs_mcp_settings at activation and never used.\n- The Activity log stores the AI client name (from DCR or the User-Agent) but not the WordPress user ID.\n- Streamable HTTP: GET on /mcp returns 405, so there is no server-initiated stream. Sessions are created but not enforced on later requests.\n- wp_delete_media calls wp_delete_attachment, which deletes permanently on most sites (unless MEDIA_TRASH is on), even when force is not set."
